THE REGENT OF MUSI RAWAS,

Considering : Whereas women and children are among vulnerable
a. groups who tend to experience violence and therefore need to receive protection;
whereas violence against women and children
b. continues to increase, therefore protection efforts are needed;
whereas all forms of violence against women
c. and children constitute violations of law and human rights and therefore their dignity and honor need to be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their fitrah and nature without discrimination;
whereas based on the considerations as
d. referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence;

Article 45
In addition to the rights of Persons with Disabilities as referred to in paragraph (1), children with disabilities have the right to:
a. receive special Protection from Discrimination, neglect, harassment, exploitation, as well as violence and sexual crimes;
b. receive care and upbringing from family or substitute family to grow and develop optimally;
c. have their interests protected in decision-making;
d. treatment of children in a humane manner in accordance with the dignity and rights of the child;
e. Fulfillment of special needs;
f. equal treatment with other children to achieve social integration and individual development; and
g. receive social assistance.

